{
  "version": 4,
  "rule": "v4-eligibility-per-control",
  "catalog_version": "2026-11-01/v1",
  "notes": "Rule v4 pins Layer D eligibility + per-control aggregation: manufacturer-specific catalog entries apply only when the audit vehicle (trusted listing metadata) falls inside their documented make/model/year applicability; every control item (top-level plus nested controls) is interpreted independently and SAM targets the claim-relevant item. v3 cases carried no vehicle identity, so v4 re-states them with explicit vehicles and corrected expectations; v1/v2/v3 files and results are preserved as versioned history.",
  "changes_from_v3": "Dedicated-button support now requires an applicable vehicle (new insufficient cases: borrowed entries, out-of-range years, missing identity); nested controls can independently support a claim (nested-lka-supports); contradictory model context cannot override listing metadata.",
